Package: dhcp-oru-toolkit
Version: 2.0.0
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8)
Provides: dhcp-lease-list (= 2.0.0)
Conflicts: dhcp-lease-list (<< 2.0.0)
Replaces: dhcp-lease-list (<< 2.0.0)
Maintainer: labuser <labuser@dhcp-server>
Homepage: https://example.invalid/dhcp-oru-toolkit
Description: DHCP lease viewer and O-RU shared-xid forensics toolkit
 Zero-dependency (pure Python standard library) tooling for operating and
 troubleshooting DHCP for Fujitsu O-RAN radio units (O-RUs).
 .
 Ships two command-line tools:
  - dhcp-lease-list: unified ISC/Kea DHCP lease viewer (IPv4 + IPv6) with a
    --conflicts mode that flags one MAC holding multiple active IPs or one IP
    held by multiple active MACs.
  - dhcp-forensics: pure-stdlib pcap/DHCP analyzer that detects the O-RU
    DHCPv4 transaction-id (xid) reuse defect -- shared xid across units,
    reaction to foreign OFFERs, and the missing option 61 client-identifier.
 .
 The dhcp_toolkit Python package is installed under
 /usr/local/lib/dhcp-oru-toolkit and both tools are thin wrappers in
 /usr/local/sbin that run it with python3.
